      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, a developer bought large tracts of land in southern La Jolla and called the subdivision “Bird Rock – City by the Sea.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sandiegouniontribune.com/2023/10/02/bird-rock-136/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The neighborhood stayed small until the 1930s, when World War II factory workers sparked a brief housing boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sandiegouniontribune.com/2023/10/02/bird-rock-136/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A mansion in Bird Rock served as the set for MTV’s reality series “The Real World” during its 2011 San Diego shoot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
